            "low": 0,
            "high": 2,
            "choices": null
          },
          {
            "param": "rounding",
            "low": null,
            "high": null,
            "choices": [
              "trunc",
              "round"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "budget_share": 0.5,
        "why": "Pipelined is the only family that can meet the 32 MSPS throughput constraint (1 result/cycle). We search for the minimum area (LUTs+FFs) design that meets the accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12). The accuracy constraint requires ~12-13 bits, so data_width 14-20 and n_iter 12-16 cover the feasible accuracy region. We minimize area by keeping widths and iterations as low as possible while meeting accuracy."
      },
      {
        "family": "pipelined_m",
        "ranges": [
          {
            "param": "data_width",
            "low": 14,
            "high": 20,
            "choices": null
          },
          {
            "param": "n_iter",
            "low": 12,
            "high": 16,
            "choices": null
          },
          {
            "param": "angle_guard",
            "low": 0,
            "high": 2,
            "choices": null
          },
          {
            "param": "frac_guard",
            "low": 0,
            "high": 2,
            "choices": null
          },
          {
            "param": "rounding",
            "low": null,
            "high": null,
            "choices": [
              "trunc",
              "round"
            ]
          },
          {
            "param": "m",
            "low": 2,
            "high": 8,
            "choices": null
          }
        ],
        "budget_share": 0.5,
        "why": "Pipelined_m is also 1 result/cycle and can meet throughput. It uses fewer FFs than fully pipelined (registers every m stages), potentially reducing area. We search the same accuracy-feasible region to find the minimum area design. The m parameter trades off latency (ceil(N/m)+2) against area (fewer FFs)."
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "The iterative and unrolled_k families cannot meet the 32 MSPS throughput constraint due to their multi-cycle latency. Only pipelined and pipelined_m families produce 1 result/cycle and can meet the throughput requirement. We focus on the minimum area (LUTs+FFs) designs that meet the accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) and the system latency constraint (sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44 us). The system constraint requires that 32 requests issued at once must all be back within 0.44 us. For a pipelined design with 1 result/cycle, the latency is N+2 cycles. At Fmax, this must be <= 0.44 us. If Fmax is ~100 MHz (10 ns/cycle), N+2 <= 44 cycles, which is easily met for N=12-16. The main constraint is area minimization."
  }
}
